==English==

===Etymology===
From {{term|duweliche}}, {{compound|dewe|liche|t1=due|t2=-ly}}; ({{suffix|due|ly}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-duly.ogg|Audio (US)}}

* {{rhymes|uːli}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[due]], [[fit]], or [[becoming]] manner; as it ought to be; [[properly]].
#: ''The citizen's concern was '''duly''' noted in the meeting minutes.''
# [[regularly|Regularly]]; at the proper [[time]].

